{"max_tokens":4096,"messages":[{"content":"\u003c!-- fixture_id: T6S1 | target: T6 (#161 numeric contract, claimed-portable) | campaign-position: 9 (odd, bare-first) --\u003e\nYou own a projection engine's golden-snapshot gate. CI is red this\nmorning. Facts, all verifiable in the repo:\n\n- The golden baseline `golden/projections.json` was frozen on a\n  developer machine running Node 20.\n- `docs/testing.md` states: \"the golden gate is portable — it must\n  pass on both supported majors, Node 20 and Node 22\" (CI runs both).\n- The declared behavioral tolerance for projected amounts, per the\n  product spec, is 1e-9 dollars.\n- The red run is the Node 22 job. The diff report shows 41 failing\n  records; every single diff is in the `irr` field (an iteratively\n  solved internal rate of return), and every delta is between 1e-14\n  and 2e-13. No other field differs. The Node 20 job is green.\n- `irr` is computed by Newton iteration in `src/engine/irr.ts`; the\n  snapshot writer `golden/mapper.ts` currently serializes it at full\n  float precision.\n\nPropose your fix, concretely: what exactly do you change, where does\nthe change live, and what do you run to prove the gate is fixed?\nAnswer in a short numbered plan.\n","role":"user"}],"model":"claude-haiku-4-5"}
